 ],
 "summary": "Numerical-control language for machine tools and 3D printers: each block holds letter-addressed words (G preparatory, M miscellaneous, X/Y/Z coordinates, F feed) applied in modal groups; RS274NGC adds parameters, expressions and O-code subroutines and loops. ISO 6983-1 and EIA RS-274-D are the base standards; vendors (Fanuc, Heidenhain, Marlin) define dialects.",
 "homepage": "https://linuxcnc.org/docs/html/gcode/overview.html",
 "file_extensions": [
  ".ngc",
  ".nc",
  ".gcode",
  ".tap"
 ],
 "level_notes": {
  "1": "ISO 6983-1:2009 is paywalled; the NIST RS274NGC report and LinuxCNC manual are the open references.",
  "2": "Tutorials are mostly machinist and hobbyist blog posts; the LinuxCNC manual doubles as the tutorial."
 },
